WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:01.834
[music playing]

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:03.135
HOST: Congratulations,
bladesmiths.

00:00:03.202 --> 00:00:04.704
You made it through
to the final round,

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:06.439
but your work is far from over.

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:07.974
Now we're sending
you back to your home

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:10.677
forge to create an iconic
blade from history--

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:15.748
the kora.

00:00:15.848 --> 00:00:18.484
[nervous laughter]

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:20.620
HOST (VOICEOVER): The kora
sword originated in Nepal, where

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:23.055
it was wielded for centuries
by a legendary group

00:00:23.122 --> 00:00:25.357
of soldiers, the Gurkhas.

00:00:25.424 --> 00:00:28.061
The Gurkhas were known for
their fearless military prowess

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:29.461
of weapons-based
martial arts, which

00:00:29.528 --> 00:00:32.531
included symbolic weaponry
like the kora sword.

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:34.967
This fearsome sword features
a long, curved blade

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:37.404
that flares outward
at the tip, maximizing

00:00:37.504 --> 00:00:40.607
the force of each swing and
making it an ideal weapon

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:43.176
for both slashing and chopping.

00:00:43.242 --> 00:00:45.978
Also used in sacrifice,
a skilled kora

00:00:46.078 --> 00:00:48.514
wielder could reportedly
cut a sheep in half

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:49.582
with just one swing.

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:55.121
HOST: It must be an
effective, working version

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:57.323
of that deadly weapon.

00:00:57.423 --> 00:01:02.428
It must include a spatulated
hook tip, a guard, and pommel.

00:01:02.528 --> 00:01:06.132 line:8%
 Josh has definitely
never made a kora before,

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:08.000
and neither have I.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:09.469
HOST: You will have
five days at your home

00:01:09.536 --> 00:01:11.471
forge to complete
this challenge.

00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:12.872
At the end of five
days, you will

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:14.641
return to present
your finished koras

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:16.609
to our panel of expert judges.

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:19.445
Only after they've subjected
those weapons to a series

00:01:19.511 --> 00:01:22.247
of brutal tests will
they declare one of you

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:23.749
the "Forged in
Fire" champion who

00:01:23.816 --> 00:01:26.151
gets that check for $10,000.

00:01:26.218 --> 00:01:27.253
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:29.588
We'll see you in five days.

00:01:29.655 --> 00:01:30.323
 Good luck.

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:31.224
 You too.

00:01:35.594 --> 00:01:37.230
 It's day one at my
home forge, and I'm

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:41.300
hoping to get accomplished
the rough forging of my blade.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.803
I've never made any
blade this long before,

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:46.072
so it's going to
be an adventure.

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:50.043
Josh has more to lose
because he is a master smith.

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:51.944
I really hope that he
doesn't underestimate

00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:55.448
me during this challenge.

00:01:55.514 --> 00:01:59.017
I'm going to try to stay
pretty historically accurate.

00:01:59.118 --> 00:02:00.854
I'm going to be
forging Damascus,

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:03.288
and having that Damascus
on a large blade

00:02:03.355 --> 00:02:05.125
will really be pretty cool.

00:02:08.861 --> 00:02:12.365
This is the biggest build
of Damascus I've ever made.

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:16.069
As I'm forging out the Damascus,
I'm realizing it's way too big,

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:18.704
and I can't actually
hold it correctly

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:20.272
because it's too long.

00:02:20.339 --> 00:02:23.609
Everything about this big
billet is taking a lot of time--

00:02:23.709 --> 00:02:26.746
me swinging it from
the forge to the press

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:29.448
and drawing it out and
waiting for it to heat up.

00:02:29.515 --> 00:02:31.417
I'm going to have to
speed things up tomorrow.

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:40.059
 Yesterday, got the blade
all forged, the Damascus made.

00:02:40.126 --> 00:02:42.261
So today, I hope to
get it all profiled

00:02:42.327 --> 00:02:44.364
and successfully heat treated.

00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:47.367 line:8%
And I'd like to grind
a fuller in this blade.

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:49.636 line:8%
I think in order to beat
this kid, I got to do

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:52.538 line:14%
some things that he won't.

00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:54.373
This groove will take a
little bit of weight out,

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:57.177
but more than anything,
I think it's cool.

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:03.282
Groove looks pretty good.

00:03:03.382 --> 00:03:05.952
Today's probably the most
critical day of the five.

00:03:06.018 --> 00:03:07.219
Here goes nothing.

00:03:07.286 --> 00:03:09.321
If the heat treat
fails, it's a couple

00:03:09.421 --> 00:03:10.924
of days worth of lost work.

00:03:18.163 --> 00:03:19.398
Seems to be hard.

00:03:19.498 --> 00:03:21.067
Generally, you heat
treat and grind

00:03:21.134 --> 00:03:23.836
an edge on a sword or
a blade based on what

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:25.171
it's going to be used for.

00:03:25.238 --> 00:03:26.806
And I don't know what
it's going to be used.

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:27.941
For that's the problem.

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:36.582
 Today, I'm going
to do my heat treat.

00:03:36.648 --> 00:03:38.151
Unfortunately, I don't
have a heat treating

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:39.819
oven large enough, so
I'm going to have to do

00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:42.554
this in the propane forge.

00:03:42.621 --> 00:03:47.326
Yeah, this sword is at least
twice as big as I'm used to.

00:03:47.426 --> 00:03:51.430
I would not normally heat
treat something like this.

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:54.900
Hopefully this thing
heats up evenly.

00:03:54.967 --> 00:03:56.769
OK, go for the quench.

00:04:03.876 --> 00:04:04.844
It's perfectly straight.

00:04:04.944 --> 00:04:06.446
It's really hardened.

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:09.649
And now I'm going to sharpen
it, and then I'll do my testing.

00:04:18.991 --> 00:04:20.192
Worked pretty good.

00:04:20.292 --> 00:04:23.095
Josh better bring his
A-game to beat this.

00:04:23.195 --> 00:04:24.730 line:14%
Good boy.

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:28.334 line:8%
JOSH: All right, we'll try a
test out here of this edge.

00:04:28.401 --> 00:04:29.268
It's day four.

00:04:29.368 --> 00:04:32.071
My blade is done.

00:04:32.138 --> 00:04:33.606
That thing really
sticks in there.

00:04:33.672 --> 00:04:35.908
I don't know what Liam's
blade's looking like right now,

00:04:35.975 --> 00:04:38.343
but it's hard to imagine
that he's got anything

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:39.378
going better than mine.

00:04:39.444 --> 00:04:42.481
I'm feeling really confident.

00:04:42.548 --> 00:04:47.086
The handle-- probably my last
big hurdle on this sword.

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:49.422
Getting ready to put
my handle in the acid

00:04:49.522 --> 00:04:52.625
here to etch the Damascus.

00:04:52.725 --> 00:04:55.094
Looks pretty cool.

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:56.896
That handle should be
about bulletproof--

00:04:56.962 --> 00:04:58.597
screwed and glued.

00:04:58.698 --> 00:05:00.600
I don't think there's any
more I could have done.

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:01.800
This is my best.

00:05:01.901 --> 00:05:06.472
Win or lose, I created
something that most people

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:08.907
can't, so I'm proud of that.

00:05:09.007 --> 00:05:12.545
 The Nepalese kora was a blade
that had the distinct inward

00:05:12.612 --> 00:05:14.813
curve and the spatula
could flare at the tip,

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:17.416
making it a weapon for
slicing and chopping.

00:05:17.483 --> 00:05:19.385
And we'll cut across
these sandbags.

00:05:19.485 --> 00:05:21.454
That'll see how sharp
your blades are.

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:22.821
Josh, you're up first.
Are you ready?

00:05:22.888 --> 00:05:23.589
 I'm ready.

00:05:23.656 --> 00:05:24.122
Let's do it.

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:41.140
[music playing]

00:05:41.207 --> 00:05:42.808
 Josh, great balance.

00:05:42.875 --> 00:05:45.811
The blade really wants
to chop and slice.

00:05:45.911 --> 00:05:48.180
The recovery of the
blade makes it one that

00:05:48.246 --> 00:05:49.816
wants to continue for combat.

00:05:49.916 --> 00:05:52.852
One problem I have
here is this handle.

00:05:52.918 --> 00:05:54.252
It tends to roll.

00:05:54.353 --> 00:05:56.889
But other than
that, it will cut.

00:05:56.956 --> 00:05:57.623
Good job, sir.

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:58.624
 Thank you.

00:05:58.690 --> 00:05:59.992
 Liam, you're up next.
Are you ready?

00:06:00.059 --> 00:06:00.760
 Yeah.

00:06:00.827 --> 00:06:14.773
[music playing]

00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:17.476
 When you said that this was
heavy, you weren't kidding.

00:06:17.576 --> 00:06:19.245
This is a chopper.

00:06:19.311 --> 00:06:21.680
A little hard to
control on the recoil,

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:24.383
but not enough to
where I can't wield it.

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:27.186
This, sir, will cut.

00:06:27.286 --> 00:06:27.953
 Great.

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:29.021
 Good job.

00:06:29.121 --> 00:06:31.190
Next up is a strength test.

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:32.624
Dave?

00:06:32.725 --> 00:06:34.727
DAVE: Gentlemen, to test
the strength of your kora,

00:06:34.827 --> 00:06:38.063
I'm going to take one
blow into these skulls.

00:06:38.164 --> 00:06:38.964
Josh, you're up.

00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:39.765
Are you ready?

00:06:39.832 --> 00:06:40.565
 I'm ready.

00:06:40.632 --> 00:06:41.333
DAVE: All right, fantastic.

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:55.581
[music playing]

00:06:55.648 --> 00:06:56.715
 Nice.

00:06:56.816 --> 00:06:59.585
DAVE: Josh, it went right
into the skull, swings

00:06:59.651 --> 00:07:04.457
easy, super lightweight,
but like Doug said,

00:07:04.557 --> 00:07:07.159
the handle wants
to roll in my hand.

00:07:07.259 --> 00:07:09.195
Nonetheless, nicely done.

00:07:09.262 --> 00:07:10.329
JOSH: Thank you.

00:07:10.396 --> 00:07:11.864
DAVE: All right, moving on.

00:07:11.931 --> 00:07:12.598
You ready?

00:07:12.665 --> 00:07:13.265
 Yeah.

00:07:13.365 --> 00:07:14.766
DAVE: OK.

00:07:14.866 --> 00:07:16.668
 I feel really
confident in my blade.

00:07:16.769 --> 00:07:19.839
If Josh's can do it, then
mine will do it as well.

00:07:19.906 --> 00:07:29.381
[music playing]

00:07:29.448 --> 00:07:32.852
 Wow, it's a beast.

00:07:32.919 --> 00:07:34.386
It feels really
nice in the hand.

00:07:34.453 --> 00:07:36.088
You did a great
job on this handle.

00:07:36.189 --> 00:07:39.825
Obviously, we pretty much
took care of that skull.

00:07:39.925 --> 00:07:43.295
Now, this thing, once you get
it started, it's going to go.

00:07:43.395 --> 00:07:44.363
LIAM: Right.

00:07:44.429 --> 00:07:46.432
 My only worry is stopping it.

00:07:46.532 --> 00:07:48.033
You don't always have
to have a heavy blade

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:51.637
to make a heavy blow, but
it's a beautiful piece.

00:07:51.737 --> 00:07:53.038
It's a nice job.
LIAM: Thank you.

00:07:53.138 --> 00:07:53.873
 Well done.

00:07:55.975 --> 00:08:00.078
HOST: Liam, Josh, both of
your weapons are spectacular.

00:08:00.145 --> 00:08:04.350
But in this competition, there
can only be one champion,

00:08:04.450 --> 00:08:11.890
and that champion is Liam.

00:08:11.991 --> 00:08:12.892
Congratulations.

00:08:12.992 --> 00:08:14.894
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:08:14.994 --> 00:08:18.865
Josh, unfortunately, your
blade did not make the cut.

00:08:18.931 --> 00:08:20.266
Dave will explain.

00:08:20.332 --> 00:08:23.002
DAVE: Josh, we've never seen
two weapons so evenly matched,

00:08:23.068 --> 00:08:28.106
and our decision came down to
one incredibly small thing,

00:08:28.173 --> 00:08:30.575
and it was the fact that that
handled torqued in Doug's

00:08:30.642 --> 00:08:32.211
hand, torqued in mine.

00:08:32.277 --> 00:08:34.513
It's an amazing piece of work.

00:08:34.579 --> 00:08:36.215
You should be
incredibly proud of it.

00:08:36.281 --> 00:08:38.517
I mean, I wish I could own it.

00:08:38.584 --> 00:08:41.687
HOST: Josh, please
surrender your weapon.

00:08:41.754 --> 00:08:43.255
JOSH (VOICEOVER): I came
here to challenge myself,

00:08:43.321 --> 00:08:46.625
and I came here to hopefully
represent bladesmithing well,

00:08:46.692 --> 00:08:48.427
and I think I did that.

00:08:48.493 --> 00:08:50.129
I'm disappointed in
the judges' decision,

00:08:50.196 --> 00:08:52.632
but I'm satisfied with
the kora that I produced.

00:08:52.732 --> 00:08:55.234
I'm going home to my kids,
which is where I'm happiest,

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:56.501
so that's where I want to be.

00:08:56.568 --> 00:08:57.670
 Liam, congratulations.

00:08:57.770 --> 00:08:59.338
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion

00:08:59.438 --> 00:09:01.907
and will be receiving
a check for $10,000.

00:09:01.974 --> 00:09:02.942
Good job.

00:09:03.008 --> 00:09:05.177
 You are our youngest
champion so far.

00:09:05.244 --> 00:09:06.044
Congratulations.

00:09:06.111 --> 00:09:06.845
Great job.

00:09:06.912 --> 00:09:08.547
 Good job.

00:09:08.613 --> 00:09:09.715
LIAM (VOICEOVER):
I just won "Forged

00:09:09.782 --> 00:09:11.617
in Fire," which is-- wow.

00:09:11.717 --> 00:09:14.553
This is a big feat
for me to accomplish

00:09:14.653 --> 00:09:16.088
against a master smith.

00:09:16.155 --> 00:09:18.056
I think that all the people
that I went to high school

00:09:18.156 --> 00:09:22.194
with-- they'll finally
realize it's not just a hobby.

00:09:22.261 --> 00:09:25.130
It's something that I
can really succeed at.

00:09:25.197 --> 00:09:27.166
I'm going to use the
$10,000 and just put

00:09:27.266 --> 00:09:28.467
it straight into a new shop.

00:09:28.533 --> 00:09:31.737
And these are like my
only pair of jeans,

00:09:31.837 --> 00:09:34.707
so maybe I'll get
another pair of jeans.

